<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>false</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <WarnOn>3390;$(WarnOn)</WarnOn>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <!-- 0.1.0 (2026-08-22): the first version this substrate is packed and consumed at, rather
         than compiled as source inside its first consumer's project. 0.x pre-1.0 posture: the
         public surface may still move, and a change to it advances this number IN THE SAME
         COMMIT — a folder feed keys packages by id and version, so repacking an unchanged
         version swaps the contract under every pinned consumer while their extracted caches keep
         serving the old bits. That producer-side rule is the point of the boundary: an
         in-project source file can absorb a surface change silently, a package cannot.

         0.2.0 (2026-08-22): the provider seam answered against its SECOND binding. A MINOR bump
         and unambiguously breaking, which is the point of taking it before the package is
         published rather than after. `EvalCompletion` gained a type parameter and lost
         `OutputText`; its six usage counters moved into an `EvalUsage` record carried as an
         OPTION, because a provider that reports none must not be indistinguishable from one that
         ran free. `IEvalProvider` gained the same parameter and now takes a single `EvalRequest`
         carrying a CALLER-SUPPLIED invocation key, so a replay looks up by what the harness
         considers one invocation instead of by a rule the seam guessed. `DemandCensus.printReport`
         gained a `ReportLabels` argument for the four lines only a domain can word. See DECISIONS
         D9 and D10.

         0.3.0 (2026-08-22): the substrate owns the BYTES of the artefacts it already typed. A
         MINOR bump and purely ADDITIVE — three new modules (`EvalJson`, `EvalCell`,
         `SidecarCodec`), no existing type, member, signature or printed string changed — so a
         consumer that raises the pin and adopts nothing compiles unchanged and writes the same
         files. It closes the two gaps the second consumer's bootstrap recorded: there was no
         typed result-cell record and no writer or reader for one, so each harness hand-rolled the
         field names the census keys off; and the re-gate sidecar row was typed with no codec, so
         one documented artefact acquired one spelling per harness. See DECISIONS D12. -->
    <Version>0.3.0</Version>
    <Authors>Andrew J. Willshire</Authors>
    <Company>Diametrical Ltd</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright 2026 Diametrical Ltd</Copyright>
    <!-- Apache-2.0, decided 2026-08-22 (DECISIONS D11, superseding D5's deliberate hold). The
         repository was written to a public standard from its first commit precisely so that
         choosing a licence would be a one-line act; this is that line. -->
    <PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/fuaran-ui/fuaran-eval</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/fuaran-ui/fuaran-eval</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
